# ── Irises — LOCAL dev .env (overrides + local secrets) ──────────────
# Copy to `.env` for local development (`npm run dev`). This file is gitignored.
#
# Your baseline config (models, pacing, background-job intervals, bot numbers, etc.)
# comes from deploy/app.env — the SAME committed file prod uses — which is loaded first.
# This local .env is layered ON TOP and OVERRIDES it, so put here ONLY:
#   (1) your local/dev API keys, and
#   (2) the handful of values that MUST differ locally (see below).
# Don't duplicate the deploy/app.env knobs here — edit those in deploy/app.env so the
# change applies both locally and (on push) in prod.

# ── Local-only overrides (these SHOULD differ from prod) ──
DATA_BACKEND=memory                 # no Supabase needed locally (data resets on restart)
AUTONOME_ENABLED=false              # ⚠️ KEEP OFF locally — ON sends REAL proactive messages
EMAIL_BACKSTOP_ENABLED=false        # ⚠️ KEEP OFF locally — ON judges Gmail + can message you
# Leave GMAIL_PUBSUB_TOPIC unset locally — Gmail push stays OFF without it.
NODE_ENV=development
# Point these at your ngrok tunnel (ngrok http 3000) if you exercise Gmail OAuth locally:
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://YOUR-NGROK.ngrok-free.app
GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=https://YOUR-NGROK.ngrok-free.app/oauth/google/callback

# ── Channels ──
# Web debug chat (talk to Irises in the browser — no Linq/iMessage setup needed). Served from web/.
WEB_ENABLED=true
# WEB_DEBUG_HANDLE=web:guest        # synthetic single-user identity for the web debug channel
# WEB_DEBUG_CHAT_ID=web:debug       # synthetic chat id the web channel routes to
# iMessage via Linq Blue — set LINQ_API_TOKEN below + LINQ_AGENT_BOT_NUMBERS in deploy/app.env.
# Telegram (prepared skeleton — off by default; see docs/CHANNELS.md to enable):
TELEGRAM_ENABLED=false
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Local/dev secrets (never committed) ──
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Optional — only if you exercise these paths locally:
LINQ_API_TOKEN=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
DEBUG_TOKEN=                        # gates /debug and the web chat channel; unset = localhost-only
DASHBOARD_PASSWORD=                 # password for the /dashboard admin GUI; unset = localhost-only (set a strong one in prod)
GMAIL_PUSH_VERIFY_TOKEN=            # shared secret for the /webhook/gmail Pub/Sub push (set in prod)

# Need to override a baseline knob just for local? You can add any key from deploy/app.env
# here (e.g. OPS_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5 to test cheaper) — it wins over deploy/app.env.
# Ops tuning + model experiments (defaults live in deploy/app.env): OPS_MAX_TOKENS, OPS_THINKING
# (adaptive|off), OPS_EFFORT (low|medium|high|xhigh|max), OPS_CACHE_SYSTEM, OPS_TEMPERATURE, and
# OPS_PROVIDER=openrouter + OPS_MODEL_OPENROUTER=<model> to A/B a different model via OpenRouter.
# Ops failure escalation (second look on a stronger model when a run fails): OPS_ESCALATION_ENABLED
# (false = shadow mode, triage-only), OPS_ESCALATION_PROVIDER/_MODEL/_MODEL_OPENROUTER,
# OPS_ESCALATION_TIMEOUT_MS, and OPS_ESCALATION_THINKING/_EFFORT/_CACHE_SYSTEM/_MAX_TOKENS/
# _TEMPERATURE (mirror the OPS_* knobs; MAX_TOKENS falls back to OPS_MAX_TOKENS).
# Ops transient-error retry (cheap same-role second pass for an llm_error before/instead of escalation):
# OPS_RETRY_ENABLED (default true; false = a transient error degrades to the "transient snag" beat, no retry).
# Ops progress reporting: OPS_PROGRESS_QUIET_MS (silence before first ping, default 300000),
# OPS_PROGRESS_GAP_MS (min spacing between pings, default 300000), OPS_MAX_PROGRESS_PINGS (hard cap
# on mid-run updates across all legs, default 1).
# Autonome scheduled Ops runs (defaults in deploy/app.env): AUTONOME_OPS_TIMEOUT_MS (per-run cap,
# must stay under the 5-min stale window; falls back to OPS_TASK_TIMEOUT_MS then 240000) and
# AUTONOME_DUP_DEFER_MS (how far to defer a scheduled run when the identical research is already
# running live, default 300000).
# Email judging cadence (defaults in deploy/app.env): JUDGE_DAILY_ENABLED (daily digest on/off),
# JUDGE_DIGEST_HOUR (local hour it fires, default 8), JUDGE_REALTIME_ENABLED (default false —
# true also surfaces each important email the moment it lands), JUDGE_INACTIVE_DAYS (default 3).
# Cost guards (defaults in deploy/app.env): LLM_DAILY_TOKEN_CAP, OPS_DAILY_TOKEN_CAP,
# JUDGE_DAILY_TOKEN_CAP, OPS_TASK_TOKEN_BUDGET, OPS_WEB_SEARCH_ENABLED/MAX_USES,
# OPENROUTER_MAX_TOOL_CALLS_DEFAULT, OPENROUTER_MAX_PRICE_PROMPT/_COMPLETION.
# OPENROUTER_CREDITS_WARN_USD=5     # /dashboard LLM tab turns the OpenRouter balance card red below this ($)
